  "ecological_interpretation": "The Palmer decline is nearly synchronous at the island-to-archipelago scale, but substantially more temporal compensation is retained among subcolonies within islands. This locates the main observable buffering structure below the island level: islands do not strongly insure one another against the regional decline, whereas internal breeding-patch components fluctuate more independently. The result provides a hierarchical interpretation of the N_eff association without converting it into a causal mechanism."
